{
  "family": "manager-foray",
  "note": "#924 (A-42's Swift half): a lock-screen or car scrub or skip during a CLIP of a native Foray is on the FORAY's clock, the clock Now Playing publishes (forayMediaView), never the clip's source seconds. Engine target: runner.js engineRemoteSurface hands the press to the engine's own seekTo / seekBy, the commands that branch on forayTransport (reference-engine.js _forayScrub / _forayNudge); natively the Swift driver feeds it to EngineCore.onRemote as changePlaybackPosition / skipForward / skipBackward, so these pin the remote press to the page command. narration-skip.json holds the presses during a line; this file holds the clip-side scrubs the issue names (a scrub past the current clip's out-point, a scrub before its in-point) and a skip from a clip's tail into a rendered line. Foray clock: s0 0-100 (source 100-200), n1 (spoken, 32 s) 100-132, s1 132-232 (source 300-400), n2 (rendered, 32 s) 232-264, s2 264-364 (source 500-600). JVM: the family is owed whole to A-40 (Foray transport).",
